---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="AMAKEUR｜野造 — independent digital studio founded by a non-programmer. Amateur at code. Serious about making."
>
  <article class="relative container-site py-12 sm:py-16">
    <!-- Vertical spine -->
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute left-2 top-16 hidden h-[28rem] lg:block" aria-hidden="true">
      <p class="spine">AMAKEUR</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.15fr] lg:gap-16">
      <header class="animate-fade-up lg:pt-4">
        <p class="mb-3 font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--color-fg-subtle)]">
          Studio / 关于
        </p>
        <h1 class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-[clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4rem)] leading-[0.95] tracking-[-0.04em]">
          About<br /><em class="not-italic text-[var(--color-accent)]">AMAKEUR</em>｜野造
        </h1>
        <blockquote class="mt-8 border-l-2 border-[var(--color-accent)] pl-5 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-2xl leading-snug tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--color-fg)] sm:text-3xl">
          I don't code.<br />I <em class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">make.</em>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[13px] text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">
          Amateur at code. Serious about making.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-amakeur animate-fade-up delay-1 max-w-none">
        <p>
          <strong>AMAKEUR｜野造</strong> is an independent digital studio founded by someone who does not
          primarily write code. The name is intentional: <em>amateur</em> as in lover of the craft —
          not as an apology.
        </p>
        <p>
          We ship software, games, websites, tools, and unnamed experiments. The method is unorthodox
          on purpose: natural language, AI, aesthetics, curiosity, and a bit of wild-path energy
          （野造）. If a thing wants to exist, we find a way to make it — without waiting for
          permission from a programming degree.
        </p>

        <div class="my-8 grid gap-4 border-y border-[var(--color-border)] py-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-fg-subtle)]">EN</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] !mb-0">
              Coding is one instrument. Making is the practice.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-mono)] text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-fg-subtle)]">中</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] !mb-0">
              写代码只是手段。造物才是正事。
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          We care about the feeling of a product — the silence between interactions, the honesty of a
          sentence, the small delight that doesn't need a changelog.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Amateur at code. Serious about making.</strong> That is not a slogan to soften
          expectations. It is a filter: we would rather ship something slightly imperfect and alive
          than something polished and empty.
        </p>

        <h2>What we work on</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/apps">Apps</a> — private utilities and quiet software</li>
          <li><a href="/games">Games</a> — playable sketches of ordinary life</li>
          <li><a href="/web">Web</a> — interactive and experimental sites</li>
          <li><a href="/labs">Labs</a> — vibecoding without a category</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Voice</h2>
        <p>
          Honest. Craft-serious. Slightly self-deprecating. Chinese and English both welcome.
          No AI-slop marketing. No fake scarcity. If we don't know yet, we say so.
        </p>
        <p>
          Production home: <a href="https://amakeur.com">{SITE.domain}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
